document.currentScript.insertAdjacentHTML('afterend', "<script class=\"quarto-plot-descriptions\" type=\"application/json\">{\"Acceptor\": \"The fragment LUMO that receives electrons from the occupied orbitals of the complex.\", \"Alpha electrons $N_\\\\alpha$\": \"Number $N_\\\\alpha$ of electrons with alpha spin; $M_S=(N_\\\\alpha-N_\\\\beta)/2$.\", \"Applied screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$\": \"Screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$ used in the last iteration to set the exchange fraction $\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$.\", \"Approach angle $\\\\theta\\\\;[{}^\\\\circ]$\": \"Angle $\\\\theta$ of the line from the product ring's $\\\\ce{C5-C6}$ midpoint to the ethene centre above the diene plane; $\\\\theta=0^\\\\circ$ is coplanar and $\\\\theta=90^\\\\circ$ is directly above the product bond.\", \"Approach distance $r\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance $r$ of the ethene centre from the midpoint of the $\\\\ce{C5-C6}$ bond of the completed product ring.\", \"APT charge $q\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"The atomic polar tensor charge $q_A=\\\\frac{1}{3}\\\\operatorname{tr}\\\\left(\\\\partial\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}/\\\\partial\\\\mathbf{R}_A\\\\right)$ measures the average dipole response to atomic displacement and is less basis-set dependent than Mulliken charges.\", \"Atoms\": \"A heavy atom, by element and its number in the input, together with the hydrogens bonded to it, written as the list of its atoms, such as $\\\\ce{C1}, \\\\ce{H7}, \\\\ce{H8}$. Groups with $w_A<1\\\\%$ in every orbital set shown are summed as the rest of their fragment.\", \"Atom pairs\": \"Pairs of an atom $A$ of one fragment and an atom $B$ of the other whose terms $S_{A,B}$ are summed, grouped by their role in the reaction.\", \"Partial charge $q\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"Partial charge of the atom recorded in the structure file, in elementary charges.\", \"Basis functions\": \"Number of atom-centred functions $\\\\chi_\\\\mu$ from which the molecular orbitals $\\\\psi_i=\\\\sum_\\\\mu c_{\\\\mu i}\\\\chi_\\\\mu$ are built.\", \"Basis set\": \"The family of atom-centred functions in which the orbitals are expanded; larger sets approach the complete-basis limit.\", \"Beta electrons $N_\\\\beta$\": \"Number $N_\\\\beta$ of electrons with beta spin; $M_S=(N_\\\\alpha-N_\\\\beta)/2$.\", \"$\\\\Delta d_k\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Change $\\\\Delta d_k=d_k^{(2)}-d_k^{(1)}$ of the length of bond $k$ between the two structures compared.\", \"$d_k\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Length of bond $k$.\", \"Bonds\": \"Atoms the input bonds to this one, each with its bond order, from which Gaussian builds the redundant internal coordinates; each bond is listed once, under its first atom.\", \"Calculation\": \"The calculation whose results the plotted values are.\", \"CCSD energy\": \"Total energy from coupled cluster with single and double excitations.\", \"CCSD(T) energy\": \"Total energy from CCSD with perturbative triples, often called the gold standard of single-reference quantum chemistry.\", \"Charge change $\\\\Delta q\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"The atomic charge change on excitation is $\\\\Delta q_A=-\\\\int_A\\\\Delta\\\\rho\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$, integrated over the region nearer its nucleus than any other. Positive values indicate electron loss.\", \"CIS energy\": \"Total energy of the excited state from configuration interaction with single excitations.\", \"Program terminated normally\": \"Whether the program reached its normal completion record; a tick marks a complete output, a cross an error termination, and an hourglass an output still running, pending or otherwise unfinished.\", \"$\\\\left\\\\lVert \\\\mathbf{F}\\\\mathbf{D}\\\\mathbf{S}-\\\\mathbf{S}\\\\mathbf{D}\\\\mathbf{F}\\\\right\\\\rVert_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Root-mean-square of the commutator of the Fock and density matrices, $\\\\mathbf{F}\\\\mathbf{D}\\\\mathbf{S}-\\\\mathbf{S}\\\\mathbf{D}\\\\mathbf{F}$, which vanishes at self-consistency.\", \"$w\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"The share in percent of the part chosen above the matrices: each atom group's share $w_A$ of the whole orbital, its share $w_{A,l}$ of the functions of angular momentum $l$, or for one atom its $w_{A,l}$ of each $l$.\", \"Configurations\": \"The single excitations that make up the state, with their weights.\", \"$V_\\\\rho\\\\;[a_0^{3}]$\": \"Volume enclosed by the density contour used to define the molecule's size in the screening model.\", \"Convergence check $n_{\\\\mathrm{check}}$\": \"Index of a printed geometry-convergence check in output order. Gaussian's step numbers can restart when another optimization begins.\", \"Converged\": \"Whether this step met every convergence criterion the program applies.\", \"Action\": \"What the line does to the coordinate. An active coordinate is optimized, a frozen one is held at its start value, an inactive one is only defined for use in other formulas, and a scanned one is stepped through a series of constrained optimizations; others are removed, printed only, or given a numerical or set second derivative.\", \"Definition\": \"The coordinate as a formula of atom positions: $R$ a bond length, $A$ a bond angle, $D$ a dihedral angle, $L$ a linear bend, $X$, $Y$ and $Z$ Cartesian components, with the atom numbers as subscripts. Lines of one form are written once for the $n$-th line.\", \"Coordinate\": \"\\u56fa\\u6709\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $s$\\u3002\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u304b\\u3089\\u306e\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u52a0\\u91cd\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $\\\\sqrt{m_i}\\\\,x_i$ \\u3067\\u306e\\u5f27\\u9577\\u3002\", \"Label\": \"Name the input gives the coordinate, or the name Gaussian prints for it among its initial parameters. A row that joins lines of one form gives the first and the last name.\", \"Setting\": \"Settings the line gives, such as a scan's number of steps and step size, in the unit of its row.\", \"Initial value\": \"Value of the coordinate at the first geometry: as Gaussian prints it among its initial parameters, or else measured at the input geometry. It is in the unit in brackets beside the coordinate: \\u00c5 for bonds and Cartesian components and degrees for angles. A formula has its own units, since Gaussian evaluates it with bonds in bohr and angles in radians, times any constants written in it. A row that joins lines of different values leaves it empty.\", \"$x\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Cartesian $x$ coordinate of the atom, in the orientation the program printed.\", \"$y\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Cartesian $y$ coordinate of the atom, in the orientation the program printed.\", \"$z\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Cartesian $z$ coordinate of the atom, in the orientation the program printed.\", \"CPU time\": \"Processor time summed over all cores; above the wall time when the job ran in parallel.\", \"Degeneracy\": \"Number $g$ of orbitals sharing this energy, forced equal by the symmetry of the molecule: $g=2$ for an $e$ set, $g=3$ for a $t$ set.\", \"$\\\\Delta P$\": \"Change of the density between consecutive iterations.\", \"Density change $\\\\Delta\\\\rho\\\\;[a_0^{-3}]$\": \"The density change on excitation is $\\\\Delta\\\\rho=\\\\rho_{\\\\mathrm{p}}-\\\\rho_{\\\\mathrm{h}}$. It is negative (blue) where electrons leave, positive (red) where they arrive, and integrates to zero.\", \"$\\\\max\\\\lvert\\\\Delta P\\\\rvert$\": \"Largest change $\\\\max_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}\\\\lvert P^{(n)}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}-P^{(n-1)}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}\\\\rvert$ of a density-matrix element between iterations.\", \"$\\\\Delta P_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}$\": \"Root-mean-square change of the density matrix between iterations, $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{N^2}\\\\sum_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}(P^{(n)}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu}-P^{(n-1)}_{\\\\mu\\\\nu})^2}$; the SCF converges once it falls below its threshold.\", \"Dipole derivatives\": \"Derivatives $\\\\partial\\\\mu_i/\\\\partial x_j$ of the dipole moment with respect to the atomic coordinates, which give the infrared intensities and APT charges.\", \"$\\\\mu\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{D}]$\": \"Electric dipole moment $\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}=\\\\sum_A Z_A\\\\mathbf{R}_A-\\\\int\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf{r})\\\\,\\\\mathbf{r}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$ of the nuclei and electrons, in debye.\", \"Dipole transition\": \"Whether the transition dipole is allowed along the listed axes or forbidden by symmetry or spin.\", \"Dipole moment $\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}=(\\\\mu_x,\\\\mu_y,\\\\mu_z)$\": \"Electric dipole moment $\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}=\\\\sum_A Z_A\\\\mathbf{R}_A-\\\\int\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf{r})\\\\,\\\\mathbf{r}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$ as a vector in the printed orientation; zero for a molecule with inversion symmetry.\", \"$\\\\Delta q_{\\\\max}$\": \"Largest predicted coordinate change $\\\\max_i\\\\lvert\\\\Delta q_i\\\\rvert$ of the next optimization step, in Gaussian's native coordinate units (bohr for distances, radians for angles).\", \"$\\\\Delta q_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}$\": \"Root-mean-square predicted coordinate change reported by Gaussian in its native optimization coordinates (bohr for distances, radians for angles).\", \"$r_{2,3}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance between atoms $2$ and $3$.\", \"$r_{2,4}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance between atoms $2$ and $4$.\", \"$r_{3,4}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance between atoms $3$ and $4$, the central bond.\", \"$r_{3,5}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance between atoms $3$ and $5$.\", \"$r_{4,5}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance between atoms $4$ and $5$.\", \"$r_{\\\\mathrm{NH}}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u7a92\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"$r_{\\\\mathrm{OH}}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u9178\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"Electronic state\": \"Term symbol of the electronic state Gaussian archived, such as $^1A_1$: spin multiplicity and symmetry in Gaussian's point group.\", \"Electrostatic potential $V\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{V}]$\": \"Electrostatic potential $V(\\\\mathbf r)$ on the density surface. Red attracts a positive charge; blue repels it.\", \"Energy $[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Energy, converted to electronvolts.\", \"$E_n-E_N\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Energy of this optimization step relative to the last recorded check, $E_n-E_N$, where $N$ numbers the last check printed; the last check is not assumed converged.\", \"$\\\\delta E\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"Energy difference $\\\\delta E=E_2-E_1$ between the two structures compared.\", \"$E(s)-E(s_\\\\mathrm{R})\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306e\\u70b9 $s_\\\\mathrm{R}$ \\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u5dee $\\\\Delta E(s)=E(s)-E(s_\\\\mathrm{R})$\\u3002\\u305d\\u306e\\u70b9\\u304c\\u78ba\\u8a8d\\u6e08\\u307f\\u306e\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u4eee\\u5b9a\\u3057\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"$E-E(s_\\\\mathrm{R})\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411 IRC \\u306e\\u70b9\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u3002\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u3084\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u306e\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306f IRC \\u4e0a\\u306b\\u3042\\u308b\\u3068\\u306f\\u9650\\u3089\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"$E-E_{\\\\mathrm{TS}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"Energy along the reaction path relative to the transition state at its top, $E(s)-E(0)$.\", \"Enthalpy\": \"Enthalpy $H=U+pV$ of the ideal gas at the stated temperature, including the electronic-structure energy.\", \"$S_i\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{cal}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{K}^{-1}]$\": \"Contribution $S_i$ to the entropy in the ideal-gas, rigid-rotor and harmonic-oscillator model.\", \"Evaluated screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$\": \"Screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$ evaluated from the final electronic response; when it matches the applied value, the screening is self-consistent.\", \"Exact-exchange fraction $c_{\\\\mathrm{HF}}$\": \"Fraction $c_{\\\\mathrm{HF}}$ of Hartree\\u2013Fock exchange in the functional, $E_{\\\\mathrm{XC}}=c_{\\\\mathrm{HF}}E_{\\\\mathrm{X}}^{\\\\mathrm{HF}}+\\\\dots$: $c_{\\\\mathrm{HF}}=0.2$ for B3LYP, $\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$ for dielectric-dependent DFT.\", \"$\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$\": \"Exact-exchange fraction $\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$ of dielectric-dependent DFT, which sets $E_{\\\\mathrm{XC}}=\\\\alpha E_{\\\\mathrm{X}}^{\\\\mathrm{HF}}+(1-\\\\alpha)E_{\\\\mathrm{X}}^{\\\\mathrm{B88}}+\\\\sqrt{1-\\\\alpha}\\\\,E_{\\\\mathrm{C}}^{\\\\mathrm{LYP}}$.\", \"$\\\\Delta E\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Vertical excitation energy $\\\\Delta E=E_n-E_0$ of the excited state above the ground state, at the same geometry.\", \"State\": \"Singlet $S_n$ or triplet $T_n$, numbered by energy within its spin. Degenerate states share a row or level.\", \"Execution interval\": \"First and last recorded instant of the run, in Japan Standard Time; the last is the render time while the job continues.\", \"Final density change\": \"Change of the density in the last SCF iteration, a measure of how well it converged.\", \"$k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{mdyn}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"Force constant $k=\\\\partial^2E/\\\\partial Q^2$ of the normal mode $Q$, the curvature of the energy along it.\", \"$F_{\\\\max}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"Largest force component $\\\\max_i\\\\lvert F_i\\\\rvert$ with $F_i=-\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i$; every force vanishes at a stationary point.\", \"$F_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"The root-mean-square force is $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}F_i^2}$ over the Cartesian components of the $N$ atoms and indicates how far the geometry is from a stationary point.\", \"$r\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Length of a forming C\\u2013C bond at a point of the reaction path.\", \"Bond\": \"A bond that forms along the reaction path, named by its two atoms.\", \"Composition\": \"Mulliken share of each atom's functions of each angular momentum in the orbital set, $w_{A,l}=\\\\sum_{\\\\mu\\\\in A,\\\\ l_\\\\mu=l}c_\\\\mu(\\\\mathbf{S}\\\\mathbf{c})_\\\\mu$, averaged over degenerate orbitals; atoms with $w_A<1\\\\%$ are summed as other atoms, and the shares add up to $\\\\sum_A\\\\sum_l w_{A,l}=100\\\\%$.\", \"Fragment orbital\": \"Orbital of one fragment calculated alone at the same geometry, named by its position from the fragment's frontier and its symmetry under the mirror plane.\", \"Weight $w\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share of the state in this transition, $w=\\\\sum_{(i,a)\\\\in C}2c_{ia}^2$ over the set $C$ of configurations $i\\\\rightarrow a$ it groups, each restricted one standing for both spins; an unrestricted configuration counts once, $c_{ia}^2$. The shares of a state add up to about $\\\\sum_C w=100\\\\%$.\", \"Framework group\": \"Gaussian's framework group, which is the point group together with the symmetry element on which each set of equivalent atoms lies.\", \"Level\": \"Position of the orbital set from the frontier, $\\\\mathrm{HOMO}$, then $\\\\mathrm{HOMO}_{1}$, $\\\\mathrm{HOMO}_{2}$ and lower for occupied sets, $\\\\mathrm{LUMO}$, then $\\\\mathrm{LUMO}_{1}$ and higher for unoccupied ones, the subscript counting sets from the frontier; degenerate orbitals count as one set.\", \"Fragment\": \"Fragment of covalently bonded atoms, by its formula: atoms $A$ and $B$ are bonded when $d_{AB}<r_A+r_B+0.4\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}$, with $r_A$ and $r_B$ their covalent radii, so bonds still forming at a saddle separate the fragments.\", \"$S_G,\\\\ S'_G$\": \"Share of a group $G$ of atom pairs in an overlap, $S_G=\\\\sum_{(A,B)\\\\in G}S_{A,B}$ in $S$ and $S'_G$ alike in $S'$; the shares of all groups add up to the whole overlap.\", \"Overlap\": \"Overlap of a frontier pair of the fragments: $S=\\\\langle\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)|\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)\\\\rangle$ for normal and $S'=\\\\langle\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(Y)|\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(X)\\\\rangle$ for inverse electron demand, $X$ being the donor of normal demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"$\\\\psi^{(A)}\\\\psi^{(B)}\\\\;[a_0^{-3}]$\": \"Product of the two orbitals of a frontier pair, kept to a chosen group $G$ of atom pairs, $f_G=\\\\sum_{(A,B)\\\\in G}\\\\psi^{(A)}\\\\psi^{(B)}$ with $\\\\psi^{(A)}=\\\\sum_{\\\\mu\\\\in A}c_\\\\mu\\\\phi_\\\\mu$; its integral is those pairs' share of $S$ or $S'$. Blue adds to the overlap and red subtracts from it.\", \"Pair\": \"The frontier orbital pairs $S$ for normal electron demand, $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)$ with $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)$, and $S'$ for inverse demand, $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(Y)$ with $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(X)$. Here $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"$F\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}^{-1}]$\": \"Frontier term of the Klopman\\u2013Salem equation, $F=S^2/\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon+S'^2/\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon'$ with $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon=\\\\epsilon_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)-\\\\epsilon_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)$ and $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon'=\\\\epsilon_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(X)-\\\\epsilon_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(Y)$; the frontier stabilization is $\\\\Delta E\\\\approx-2k^2F$ with an unknown constant $k$. $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"Gaussian version\": \"Gaussian revision and build date, as the output prints them.\", \"Geometry source\": \"Where the job takes its starting geometry from: the coordinates in the input file, or those saved in the checkpoint by a previous job.\", \"Gibbs energy\": \"Gibbs energy $G=H-TS$ at the stated temperature and pressure, electronic energy included.\", \"$g_{\\\\max}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"Largest energy gradient $\\\\max_i\\\\lvert\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i\\\\rvert$, the largest force component.\", \"$g_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"The root-mean-square energy gradient is $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}(\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i)^2}$ over the Cartesian coordinates of the $N$ atoms and vanishes at a stationary point.\", \"$g_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u4e8c\\u4e57\\u5e73\\u5747\\u5e73\\u65b9\\u6839\\u306e\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u52fe\\u914d $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}(\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i)^2}$\\u3002$N$ \\u500b\\u306e\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u30c7\\u30ab\\u30eb\\u30c8\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u306b\\u3064\\u3044\\u3066\\u53d6\\u308a\\u3001\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u3067\\u6d88\\u3048\\u308b\\u3002\", \"$C_{V,i}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{cal}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{K}^{-1}]$\": \"Contribution $C_{V,i}$ to the constant-volume heat capacity.\", \"HOMO energy $\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{HOMO}}$\": \"Energy $\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{HOMO}}$ of the highest occupied molecular orbital (HOMO), an approximation to minus the ionization energy that depends strongly on the exact-exchange fraction.\", \"$S_{\\\\mathrm{hp}}$\": \"Overlap of where the electron leaves and where it arrives, $\\\\int\\\\sqrt{\\\\rho_{\\\\mathrm{h}}\\\\rho_{\\\\mathrm{p}}}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$: $S_{\\\\mathrm{hp}}\\\\approx1$ for a local excitation, $S_{\\\\mathrm{hp}}\\\\approx0$ for charge transfer.\", \"Imaginary frequencies\": \"Number $N_{\\\\mathrm{imag}}$ of imaginary harmonic frequencies: $N_{\\\\mathrm{imag}}=0$ at a minimum, $N_{\\\\mathrm{imag}}=1$ at a transition state.\", \"Independent functions\": \"Number of linearly independent combinations of the basis functions kept, after near-linear dependencies are removed; it equals the number of molecular orbitals.\", \"$k$\": \"\\u6700\\u521d\\u304b\\u3089\\u6570\\u3048\\u305f\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u632f\\u52d5\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u8ecc\\u9053\\u5bfe\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"$I_{\\\\mathrm{IR}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{km}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"The infrared intensity satisfies $I\\\\propto\\\\lvert\\\\partial\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}/\\\\partial Q\\\\rvert^2$ and depends on the dipole change along mode $Q$.\", \"Initial screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$\": \"Screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$ the first iteration uses to set the exchange fraction $\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$, before the molecule's own response replaces it.\", \"$n$\": \"Number of the excited state, from the lowest.\", \"Job type\": \"Kind of calculation Gaussian archived, such as SP for a single point, FOpt for an optimization or Freq for frequencies.\", \"Linked jobs\": \"Number of Gaussian jobs chained in the input, each running its own route section.\", \"LUMO energy $\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{LUMO}}$\": \"Energy $\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{LUMO}}$ of the lowest unoccupied molecular orbital (LUMO).\", \"Maximum SCF iterations\": \"Most self-consistent-field iterations allowed before the program stops without convergence.\", \"Method\": \"The density functional or wavefunction theory that approximates electron correlation.\", \"Methylene rotation $\\\\tau\\\\;[{}^\\\\circ]$\": \"Rigid rotation $\\\\tau$ of the diene's terminal methylene groups about $\\\\ce{C1=C2}$ and $\\\\ce{C4=C3}$.\", \"Mode character\": \"Imaginary modes have negative curvature; non-imaginary modes alone do not establish a minimum.\", \"$K_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{mdyn}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u529b\\u306e\\u5b9a\\u6570 $K_k=\\\\partial^2E/\\\\partial Q_k^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3002\", \"$I_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{km}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8d64\\u5916\\u5f37\\u5ea6 $I_k\\\\propto\\\\lvert\\\\partial\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}/\\\\partial Q_k\\\\rvert^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cc\\u6975\\u5b50\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30e1\\u30f3\\u30c8\\u306e\\u5909\\u5316\\u304b\\u3089\\u3002\", \"$\\\\mu_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{Da}]$\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u63db\\u7b97\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3067\\u3001\\u305d\\u306e\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u3067\\u52d5\\u304f\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u6709\\u52b9\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3002\", \"$\\\\widetilde{\\\\nu}_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{cm}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8abf\\u548c\\u6ce2\\u6570 $\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\pi c}\\\\sqrt{K_k/\\\\mu_k}$\\u3002\\u865a\\u6570\\u306e\\u5024\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u3067\\u793a\\u3057\\u3001\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u306e\\u3088\\u3046\\u306b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u304c\\u4e0b\\u304c\\u308b\\u65b9\\u5411\\u3092\\u8868\\u3059\\u3002\", \"Model\": \"The electronic-structure model, either B3LYP with fixed weights or dielectric-dependent DFT with weights set by the screening.\", \"$\\\\epsilon\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{L}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{cm}^{-1}]$\": \"The molar absorption coefficient is $\\\\epsilon=A/(c\\\\,l)$, where $A$ is absorbance, $c$ is concentration and $l$ is path length.\", \"Charge $q$\": \"The net molecular charge in elementary charges is $q=\\\\sum_A Z_A-N$, the total nuclear charge minus the number of electrons.\", \"Molecular mass $M$\": \"Mass $M=\\\\sum_A m_A$ of the molecule from its most abundant isotopes.\", \"MP2 energy\": \"Total energy with second-order M\\u00f8ller\\u2013Plesset perturbation theory, the first correlation correction beyond Hartree\\u2013Fock.\", \"Mulliken charge $q\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"Atomic charge $q_A=Z_A-\\\\sum_{\\\\mu\\\\in A}(\\\\mathbf{P}\\\\mathbf{S})_{\\\\mu\\\\mu}$ from Mulliken population analysis, which splits overlap density equally between atoms; strongly basis-set dependent.\", \"Normal termination\": \"Whether the program finished this job without an error.\", \"NTO amplitude $\\\\phi\\\\;[a_0^{\\\\frac{-3}{2}}]$\": \"The natural transition orbital $\\\\phi$, either the hole or the particle. Red and blue mark opposite signs.\", \"Pair $k$\": \"Number of the natural-transition-orbital pair, from the most important.\", \"$100\\\\eta_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $\\\\eta_k=\\\\lambda_k/\\\\sum_j\\\\lambda_j$ of the excitation carried by natural-transition-orbital pair $k$, in percent.\", \"$w_k$\": \"Weight $w_k=\\\\lambda_k/\\\\sum_j\\\\lambda_j$ of natural-transition-orbital pair $k$ in the excitation; the weights add up to $\\\\sum_k w_k=1$.\", \"Nuclear repulsion $E_{\\\\mathrm{nn}}$\": \"Electrostatic repulsion between the nuclei, $E_{\\\\mathrm{nn}}=\\\\sum_{A<B}\\\\frac{Z_AZ_B}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{R}_A-\\\\mathbf{R}_B\\\\rvert}$; it depends only on the geometry.\", \"Occupation\": \"Whether the orbital holds electrons in the ground state.\", \"Optical permittivity $\\\\varepsilon_\\\\infty$\": \"Optical permittivity $\\\\varepsilon_\\\\infty=n^2$ of the continuum solvent, from its refractive index $n$. It is the fast electronic screening that responds during a vertical excitation.\", \"Rule\": \"A rule of the ReadOptimize section, which adds atoms to the optimized set or removes them; the rules apply in order, starting from every atom.\", \"Orbital\": \"Molecular orbital, or a set of degenerate ones, labelled by its symmetry and numbered from the lowest orbital of that symmetry.\", \"$\\\\psi\\\\;[a_0^{\\\\frac{-3}{2}}]$\": \"Amplitude $\\\\psi$ of the orbital chosen in the snapshot selector, evaluated from its saved coefficients; red surfaces enclose negative values and blue ones positive values. The sign of a whole orbital is arbitrary.\", \"$\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)+\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)\\\\;[a_0^{\\\\frac{-3}{2}}]$\": \"Sum $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)+\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)$ of the donor's HOMO and the acceptor's LUMO on the starting geometry, with the sign of the LUMO chosen so that $S>0$. Blue is positive and red negative. $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"$\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)\\\\,\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)\\\\;[a_0^{-3}]$\": \"Product $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)\\\\,\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)$ of the donor's HOMO and the acceptor's LUMO at each point of the starting geometry; its integral over space is the overlap $S$. Blue is where the two orbitals have the same sign and adds to $S$, red where they differ and subtracts from it. $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"$\\\\epsilon\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Orbital energy $\\\\epsilon_i$, the eigenvalue of the Kohn\\u2013Sham or Fock equation $\\\\hat F\\\\psi_i=\\\\epsilon_i\\\\psi_i$; differences of orbital energies are not excitation energies.\", \"$\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"HOMO\\u2013LUMO gap $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon=\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{LUMO}}-\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{HOMO}}$, an orbital-energy difference rather than an optical excitation energy.\", \"HOMO\\u2013LUMO gap $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon=\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{LUMO}}-\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{HOMO}}$\": \"Difference of the frontier orbital energies, not an optical excitation energy.\", \"HOMO\\u2013LUMO gap $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon$\": \"HOMO\\u2013LUMO gap $\\\\Delta\\\\epsilon=\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{LUMO}}-\\\\epsilon_{\\\\mathrm{HOMO}}$ between the frontier orbital sets, an orbital-energy difference rather than an optical excitation energy.\", \"HOMO\\u2013LUMO overlap $S$\": \"Overlap $S=\\\\langle\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(X)|\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(Y)\\\\rangle$ of the donor's HOMO and the acceptor's LUMO at the starting geometry, each fragment calculated alone, without polarization by the other; the sign of the LUMO is chosen so that $S>0$. $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"Transition\": \"Orbital set the electron leaves and the one it enters, degenerate orbitals together, labelled by symmetry and numbered from the lowest orbital of each symmetry.\", \"$f_n$\": \"Oscillator strength $f_n=\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\Delta E_n\\\\lvert\\\\langle 0\\\\rvert\\\\hat{\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}}\\\\lvert n\\\\rangle\\\\rvert^2$ (atomic units) of the transition to state $n$. It measures how strongly the transition absorbs light, and a dark state has $f_n=0$.\", \"$f_n^{(L)}$\": \"Oscillator strength from the length form of the transition moment, $\\\\frac{2}{3}\\\\Delta E_n\\\\lvert\\\\langle 0\\\\rvert\\\\hat{\\\\mathbf{r}}\\\\lvert n\\\\rangle\\\\rvert^2$ (atomic units).\", \"$f_n^{(V)}$\": \"Oscillator strength from the velocity form of the transition moment, $\\\\langle 0\\\\rvert\\\\hat{\\\\mathbf{p}}\\\\lvert n\\\\rangle$; close agreement with the length form $f_n$ indicates a well-converged transition.\", \"$f_z$\": \"Share of the mode's motion out of the molecular plane, $f_z=\\\\sum_A\\\\Delta z_A^2/\\\\sum_A\\\\lvert\\\\Delta\\\\mathbf{r}_A\\\\rvert^2$.\", \"Forming bonds\": \"Pairs of atoms that become bonded along the reaction path: bonded at its product end and not at its reactant end.\", \"Pairs with hydrogen\": \"Pairs with a hydrogen that takes no part in a forming or breaking bond.\", \"Hydrogens\": \"Pairs with a hydrogen; in the Diels\\u2013Alder reaction, every pair that holds one of its ten hydrogens.\", \"Primary carbons\": \"The carbon pairs that become the new $\\\\sigma$ bonds of the Diels\\u2013Alder reaction, $\\\\ce{C1-C6}$ and $\\\\ce{C4-C5}$.\", \"Other reacting pairs\": \"Pairs of two atoms that each form or break a bond along the reaction path, but not with each other.\", \"Secondary carbons\": \"The diene's inner carbons, $\\\\ce{C2}$ and $\\\\ce{C3}$, each with a dienophile carbon.\", \"Spectator pairs\": \"Pairs with a heavy atom that takes no part in a forming or breaking bond, and no such hydrogen.\", \"Terminal carbons\": \"The diene's end carbons, each with the dienophile carbon it does not bond to.\", \"$\\\\sum$\": \"The whole overlap, $S$ or $S'$, the sum of every pair.\", \"$q\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"Partial charge on the atom from the population analysis, in elementary charges; it depends on how the analysis divides the density.\", \"$s\\\\;[a_0\\\\,\\\\mathrm{Da}^{\\\\frac{1}{2}}]$\": \"\\u56fa\\u6709\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $s$\\u3002\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u304b\\u3089\\u306e\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u52a0\\u91cd\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $\\\\sqrt{m_i}\\\\,x_i$ \\u3067\\u306e\\u5f27\\u9577\\u3002\", \"Structure\": \"The stationary structure of the path, such as a minimum or the saddle, whose values are marked.\", \"Geometry\": \"The nuclear geometry at which the plotted values were calculated.\", \"Point group\": \"Point group Gaussian recorded for the molecule, within its own tolerance.\", \"Point group used by Gaussian\": \"Point group detected by Gaussian within its tolerance. Printed state labels use its largest Abelian subgroup.\", \"Point group of the geometry\": \"Full point group from coordinates within $0.02\\\\,a_0$. Orbital and state labels use this group.\", \"$i$\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u70b9\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"Polarizability $\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\alpha}$\": \"The static dipole polarizability $\\\\alpha_{ij}=\\\\partial\\\\mu_i/\\\\partial\\\\mathcal{E}_j$ measures the dipole response to an electric field.\", \"$x\\\\;[a_0^{3}]$\": \"Column $x$ of the polarizability tensor $\\\\alpha_{ij}=\\\\partial\\\\mu_i/\\\\partial\\\\mathcal{E}_j$ gives the dipole induced by a field along $x$.\", \"$y\\\\;[a_0^{3}]$\": \"Column $y$ of the polarizability tensor $\\\\alpha_{ij}=\\\\partial\\\\mu_i/\\\\partial\\\\mathcal{E}_j$ gives the dipole induced by a field along $y$.\", \"$z\\\\;[a_0^{3}]$\": \"Column $z$ of the polarizability tensor $\\\\alpha_{ij}=\\\\partial\\\\mu_i/\\\\partial\\\\mathcal{E}_j$ gives the dipole induced by a field along $z$.\", \"$V_{\\\\max}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{V}]$\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u9ad8\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u9000\\u3051\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\", \"$V_{\\\\min}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{V}]$\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u4f4e\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})=\\\\sum_A\\\\frac{Z_A}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{R}_A\\\\rvert}-\\\\int\\\\frac{\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime)}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime\\\\rvert}\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u5f15\\u304d\\u5bc4\\u305b\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\", \"Pressure $p$\": \"Pressure $p$ at which the thermochemistry is evaluated, entering the translational entropy.\", \"Processors\": \"Number of processor cores the job ran on.\", \"Traceless quadrupole moment $\\\\mathbf{Q}$\": \"Traceless quadrupole moment $Q_{ij}=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\int\\\\rho_{\\\\mathrm{tot}}(3r_ir_j-r^2\\\\delta_{ij})\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$, the next term of the charge distribution after the dipole; benzene's is large along its axis.\", \"$\\\\mu\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{Da}]$\": \"The reduced mass $\\\\mu$ is the effective mass of the normal mode and enters its wavenumber as $\\\\tilde\\\\nu=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\pi c}\\\\sqrt{k/\\\\mu}$.\", \"$E-E_0\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"\\u6bd4\\u8f03\\u306e\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc $\\\\Delta E=E-E_0$\\u3002\", \"Requested CPUs per task\": \"Processor cores per task requested from the scheduler.\", \"Requested memory\": \"Memory per node requested from the scheduler, in binary units of bytes.\", \"Requested nodes\": \"Nodes requested from the scheduler.\", \"Requested partitions\": \"Scheduler partitions the job may run on, in the order the request names them.\", \"Requested tasks\": \"Tasks, one process each, requested from the scheduler.\", \"Requested wall time\": \"Wall-time limit requested from the scheduler.\", \"$\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(Y)\\\\,\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(X)\\\\;[a_0^{-3}]$\": \"Product $\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{HOMO}(Y)\\\\,\\\\psi_\\\\mathrm{LUMO}(X)$ at each point of the starting geometry; its integral over space is the overlap $S'$ of inverse electron demand. Blue adds to $S'$ and red subtracts from it. $X$ is the donor fragment of normal electron demand and $Y$ its acceptor.\", \"RMS density change\": \"Root-mean-square change of the density matrix in the last SCF iteration, which falls below the threshold at convergence.\", \"RMS force\": \"Root-mean-square force on the $N$ atoms, $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}F_i^2}$ over their Cartesian components; small at a stationary point.\", \"Rotational constants $(A,B,C)$\": \"Rotational constants $A=\\\\frac{h}{8\\\\pi^2 I_A}$, $B$ and $C$ from the principal moments of inertia $I_A\\\\leq I_B\\\\leq I_C$; two equal constants mark a symmetric top, as for benzene.\", \"$q\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u3067\\u3001\\u5404\\u70b9\\u3067\\u56fa\\u5b9a\\u3059\\u308b\\u62d8\\u675f\\u4ed8\\u304d\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u5909\\u4f4d\\u3002\", \"Last scan point\": \"Value the scanned coordinate reaches at the last step: its initial value plus the number of steps times the step size.\", \"Step size\": \"Change of the scanned coordinate between consecutive scan points, in the unit of its row.\", \"Steps\": \"Number of scan steps after the starting point; the scan optimizes the structure at each of them.\", \"$N$\": \"Number $N$ of SCF cycles the solution needed to converge, the index of its last cycle.\", \"$n_{\\\\mathrm{SCF}}$\": \"Number of the self-consistent-field solution, in output order; the job reaches one for each geometry or state it evaluates, each taking its own $N$ cycles.\", \"SCF iterations\": \"Number of self-consistent-field iterations the program needed.\", \"SCF convergence threshold\": \"Largest change of the density, or of the energy, between iterations at which the SCF counts as converged.\", \"$\\\\varepsilon_s$\": \"Molecular electronic screening $\\\\varepsilon_s$ sets $\\\\alpha=1/\\\\varepsilon_s$ in dielectric-dependent DFT. It is not bulk-liquid permittivity.\", \"$\\\\lvert\\\\Delta\\\\varepsilon_s\\\\rvert$\": \"Change $\\\\lvert\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n)}-\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n-1)}\\\\rvert$ of the screening between iterations.\", \"$\\\\varepsilon_s^{(N)}$\": \"Converged electronic screening $\\\\varepsilon_s^{(N)}$ of the molecule, from the last iteration $N$.\", \"$\\\\lvert\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n)}-\\\\varepsilon_s^{(N)}\\\\rvert$\": \"Distance $\\\\lvert\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n)}-\\\\varepsilon_s^{(N)}\\\\rvert$ of the screening of iteration $n$ from its converged value at the last iteration $N$.\", \"Screening iterated to self-consistency\": \"Whether the screening is updated from each iteration's electronic response until $\\\\varepsilon_s$ and the density agree, rather than kept fixed.\", \"$\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n)}$\": \"Screening $\\\\varepsilon_s^{(n)}$ applied in iteration $n$ to set the exchange fraction.\", \"$d\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,d}$ of the atom's $d$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$f\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,f}$ of the atom's $f$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$g\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,g}$ of the atom's $g$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$h\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,h}$ of the atom's $h$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$i\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,i}$ of the atom's $i$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$S'_G$\": \"Share of a group $G$ of atom pairs in $S'$, $S'_G=\\\\sum_{(A,B)\\\\in G}S'_{A,B}$; the shares of all groups add up to $S'$, the line $\\\\sum$.\", \"$k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,k}$ of the atom's $k$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$S_G$\": \"Share of a group $G$ of atom pairs in $S$, $S_G=\\\\sum_{(A,B)\\\\in G}S_{A,B}$; the shares of all groups add up to $S$, the line $\\\\sum$.\", \"$p\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,p}$ of the atom's $p$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$s\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_{A,s}$ of the atom's $s$ functions in the orbital.\", \"$w_A\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{\\\\%}]$\": \"Share $w_A=\\\\sum_l w_{A,l}$ of all the atom's functions in the orbital, the sum of its parts $w_{A,l}$ of each angular momentum $l$.\", \"$\\\\Delta E_{S_n}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Vertical excitation energy $\\\\Delta E_{S_n}=E(S_n)-E(S_0)$ of singlet state $S_n$ above the ground state.\", \"Slurm job\": \"Scheduler job identifier, as the run's own records report it.\", \"Solvent\": \"Solvent of the polarizable continuum model, which surrounds the molecule by a dielectric of its permittivity.\", \"Region\": \"Approximate spectral region the band falls in, a rough guide to the kind of motion or transition; the borders are conventional.\", \"Spin multiplicity $2S+1$\": \"The spin multiplicity $2S+1$, which is $1$ for a singlet, $2$ for a doublet and $3$ for a triplet. Singlets need not be closed shell.\", \"$\\\\langle S^2\\\\rangle$\": \"Spin expectation $\\\\langle S^2\\\\rangle$; deviations from the expected $S(S+1)$ indicate spin contamination.\", \"Stable\": \"Whether the SCF solution is stable, that is, whether no rotation of the orbitals lowers its energy.\", \"Initial forming bond $d_\\\\mathrm{CC}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Mean length of the two forming C\\u2013C bonds in the starting geometry.\", \"Starting geometry\": \"The geometry from which a calculation started.\", \"Static permittivity $\\\\varepsilon$\": \"Static relative permittivity $\\\\varepsilon$ of the continuum solvent, the screening of slow, equilibrated charges.\", \"$d_{\\\\max}\\\\;[a_0]$\": \"Largest predicted change of an atomic coordinate in the next step.\", \"$d_{\\\\mathrm{RMS}}\\\\;[a_0]$\": \"Root-mean-square predicted change of the atomic coordinates in the next step.\", \"Symmetry\": \"Irreducible representation describing how a mode, orbital or state transforms under the geometry's point group.\", \"Symmetry number $\\\\sigma$\": \"The rotational symmetry number $\\\\sigma$, the number of orientations of the molecule that rotation cannot distinguish; it lowers the rotational entropy by $R\\\\ln\\\\sigma$.\", \"Temperature $T$\": \"Temperature $T$ at which the thermochemistry is evaluated.\", \"Thermodynamic quantity\": \"Electronic-structure energy and zero-point corrected energy, internal energy, enthalpy and Gibbs energy at the stated conditions; these are different quantities, not electronic states.\", \"$X-E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"The quantity $X$ relative to $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$. The inferred reference inherits rounding from Gaussian's printed sums and corrections.\", \"Thermal correction to the energy\": \"Thermal correction to the energy at the stated temperature, zero-point energy included.\", \"Thermal correction $\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}$\": \"Thermal correction to internal energy, $\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}(T)=U(T)-E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}=E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}+\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{th}}(T)$. The zero-point vibrational energy is included once; $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$ includes nuclear repulsion.\", \"Thermal correction $\\\\Delta H_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}$\": \"Thermal correction to enthalpy, $\\\\Delta H_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}=H-E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}=\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}+k_{\\\\mathrm B}T$ per ideal-gas molecule.\", \"Thermal correction $\\\\Delta G_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}$\": \"Thermal correction to Gibbs energy, $\\\\Delta G_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}=G-E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}=\\\\Delta H_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}-TS$, at the stated temperature and pressure.\", \"$U_i\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{kJ}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{mol}^{-1}]$\": \"Contribution $U_i$ to the internal-energy correction at the stated temperature; the vibrational contribution includes zero-point energy. The electronic contribution here excludes the electronic-structure energy $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$.\", \"$E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}$\": \"The zero-point-corrected energy is $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}$, the electronic-structure energy including nuclear repulsion plus the harmonic zero-point vibrational correction.\", \"$U$\": \"Internal energy $U(T)=E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}(T)=E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}+\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{th}}(T)$. The thermal correction includes zero-point energy once.\", \"$H$\": \"Enthalpy $H=U+pV=E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}+k_{\\\\mathrm B}T$ per ideal-gas molecule.\", \"$G$\": \"Gibbs free energy $G=H-TS$ per molecule at the stated temperature and pressure, with electronic and zero-point energies included in $H$.\", \"Internal energy $U$\": \"Internal energy $U=E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}+\\\\Delta U_{\\\\mathrm{corr}}$, with zero-point energy included once in the correction.\", \"$E\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"Total electronic-structure energy $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$ of the SCF solution, including nuclear repulsion.\", \"$d_{\\\\mathrm{CT}}\\\\;[\\\\text{\\\\AA}]$\": \"Distance $d_{\\\\mathrm{CT}}=\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{R}_{+}-\\\\mathbf{R}_{-}\\\\rvert$ between the centroids of the density gained and lost on excitation; $d_{\\\\mathrm{CT}}\\\\approx0$ for a local excitation, large for charge transfer.\", \"$q_{\\\\mathrm{CT}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{e}]$\": \"Charge the excitation moves, $q_{\\\\mathrm{CT}}=\\\\int\\\\rho_{+}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}=\\\\int\\\\rho_{-}\\\\,\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}$, with $\\\\rho_{\\\\pm}$ the parts of $\\\\Delta\\\\rho$ above and below zero.\", \"Character\": \"Orbital types in a transition, such as $\\\\pi\\\\rightarrow\\\\pi^*$. The star denotes an antibonding orbital.\", \"Outcome\": \"Where one transition-state optimization ended. It reached either the forming saddle, with one imaginary mode that stretches both forming bonds in phase at the verified saddle's energy and bond length, or it did not converge and stopped at the optimizer's step limit.\", \"Wall time\": \"Elapsed real time of the job from start to end.\", \"$\\\\lambda\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{nm}]$\": \"Wavelength of light whose photon energy equals the excitation energy, $\\\\lambda=hc/\\\\Delta E$.\", \"$\\\\tilde\\\\nu\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{cm}^{-1}]$\": \"Harmonic wavenumber $\\\\tilde\\\\nu=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\pi c}\\\\sqrt{k/\\\\mu}$. Negative printed values indicate imaginary frequencies.\", \"$\\\\Delta\\\\widetilde{\\\\nu}_k\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{cm}^{-1}]$\": \"Difference $\\\\Delta\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k$ between the wavenumbers of mode $k$ in the two calculations compared.\", \"Zero-point correction $E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}$\": \"Harmonic zero-point vibrational energy $E_{\\\\mathrm{ZPE}}=\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sum_{k\\\\in\\\\mathcal{M}}hc\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k$ over the set $\\\\mathcal{M}$ of real modes Gaussian includes; imaginary modes are not in it.\", \"Zero-point energy\": \"Zero-point vibrational energy $\\\\frac{1}{2}\\\\sum_{k\\\\in\\\\mathcal{M}}hc\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k$ over the set $\\\\mathcal{M}$ of real harmonic modes.\", \"Closed shell\": \"A restricted reference with doubly occupied orbitals is closed shell. Equal spin counts alone do not establish this.\", \"Orbital kinetic energy $T$\": \"Orbital kinetic energy $T$; in Kohn\\u2013Sham DFT the noninteracting kinetic energy $T_s$ of the Kohn\\u2013Sham orbitals.\", \"Electron\\u2013nuclear term $V_{\\\\mathrm{ne}}$\": \"Electron\\u2013nuclear attraction $V_{\\\\mathrm{ne}}$ for all-electron calculations, not total potential energy. Effective-core potentials require separate interpretation.\", \"Coulomb and exchange\\u2013correlation $J+E_{\\\\mathrm{XC}}$\": \"The electron\\u2013electron interaction energy, the sum of the Coulomb repulsion $J$ and the exchange and correlation energy $E_{\\\\mathrm{XC}}$.\", \"Electronic energy $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$\": \"Electronic energy of the converged solution, including nuclear repulsion, not the sum of the partial components above.\", \"Virial ratio $-V/T$\": \"The dimensionless $-V/T=2$ for exact Coulombic equilibrium. Approximations can change it; it does not establish accuracy or convergence.\", \"$F\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"Largest component and root mean square of the Cartesian forces recorded at each SCF solution.\", \"Predicted coordinate step $\\\\Delta q$\": \"Predicted optimization-coordinate displacement: bohr for distances and radians for angles, not Cartesian bond-length changes.\", \"Electron Coulomb repulsion $J$\": \"Classical electron\\u2013electron Coulomb energy $J=\\\\frac12\\\\iint\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf r)\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf r\\\\prime)/|\\\\mathbf r-\\\\mathbf r\\\\prime|\\\\,\\\\mathrm d\\\\mathbf r\\\\,\\\\mathrm d\\\\mathbf r\\\\prime$. Excludes exchange and correlation.\", \"Exact-exchange contribution $c_{\\\\mathrm{HF}}E_{\\\\mathrm X}^{\\\\mathrm{HF}}$\": \"Exact-exchange contribution with weights already applied, including global and nonlocal short-range exchange. Do not multiply by the weights again.\", \"Density-functional contribution $E_{\\\\mathrm X}^{\\\\mathrm{DFT}}+E_{\\\\mathrm C}^{\\\\mathrm{DFT}}$\": \"Weighted density-functional exchange and correlation, reported together.\", \"Environment contribution\": \"Optional `env` contribution, distinct from electron\\u2013electron Coulomb energy.\", \"Program\": \"Program whose output and records the page parses, Gaussian 16 or Lotus.\", \"Projection contribution\": \"Optional `proj` contribution; it is not assigned to a chemical bond.\", \"Nonlocal exchange contribution\": \"Weighted global and short-range orbital exchange in a range-separated method, not global Hartree\\u2013Fock exchange alone.\", \"Branch\": \"Direction along the reaction path that reached the point: forward or reverse.\", \"Convergence\": \"Whether the point met its convergence criteria as Gaussian printed them; Unknown where the output does not say.\", \"Force statistic\": \"Which summary of the forces a point shows, their largest component or their root mean square.\", \"Criterion\": \"Which printed convergence criterion a point shows, the maximum or the root mean square.\", \"$F_{\\\\mathrm{c}}\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}\\\\,\\\\text{\\\\AA}^{-1}]$\": \"The limit $F_{\\\\mathrm{c}}$ Gaussian printed for this force criterion c, which the force must fall below to pass.\", \"Coordinate step limit $\\\\Delta q_{\\\\mathrm{c}}$\": \"The limit Gaussian printed for this displacement criterion, in bohr for distances and radians for angles.\", \"$X\\\\;[\\\\mathrm{eV}]$\": \"The quantity $X$ itself, as Gaussian's printed sums give it, not relative to $E_{\\\\mathrm{el}}$.\", \"point\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u70b9\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"q\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u3067\\u3001\\u5404\\u70b9\\u3067\\u56fa\\u5b9a\\u3059\\u308b\\u62d8\\u675f\\u4ed8\\u304d\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u5909\\u4f4d\\u3002\", \"nitrogen_distance\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u7a92\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"oxygen_distance\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u9178\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"energy\": \"\\u6bd4\\u8f03\\u306e\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc $\\\\Delta E=E-E_0$\\u3002\", \"path_energy\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306e\\u70b9 $s_\\\\mathrm{R}$ \\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u5dee $\\\\Delta E(s)=E(s)-E(s_\\\\mathrm{R})$\\u3002\\u305d\\u306e\\u70b9\\u304c\\u78ba\\u8a8d\\u6e08\\u307f\\u306e\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u4eee\\u5b9a\\u3057\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"comparison_energy\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411 IRC \\u306e\\u70b9\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u3002\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u3084\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u306e\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306f IRC \\u4e0a\\u306b\\u3042\\u308b\\u3068\\u306f\\u9650\\u3089\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"rms\": \"\\u4e8c\\u4e57\\u5e73\\u5747\\u5e73\\u65b9\\u6839\\u306e\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u52fe\\u914d $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}(\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i)^2}$\\u3002$N$ \\u500b\\u306e\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u30c7\\u30ab\\u30eb\\u30c8\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u306b\\u3064\\u3044\\u3066\\u53d6\\u308a\\u3001\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u3067\\u6d88\\u3048\\u308b\\u3002\", \"coordinate\": \"\\u56fa\\u6709\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cd\\u5fdc\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $s$\\u3002\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u304b\\u3089\\u306e\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u52a0\\u91cd\\u5ea7\\u6a19 $\\\\sqrt{m_i}\\\\,x_i$ \\u3067\\u306e\\u5f27\\u9577\\u3002\", \"mode\": \"\\u6700\\u521d\\u304b\\u3089\\u6570\\u3048\\u305f\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u632f\\u52d5\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u8ecc\\u9053\\u5bfe\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"frequency\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8abf\\u548c\\u6ce2\\u6570 $\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\pi c}\\\\sqrt{K_k/\\\\mu_k}$\\u3002\\u865a\\u6570\\u306e\\u5024\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u3067\\u793a\\u3057\\u3001\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u306e\\u3088\\u3046\\u306b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u304c\\u4e0b\\u304c\\u308b\\u65b9\\u5411\\u3092\\u8868\\u3059\\u3002\", \"mass\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u63db\\u7b97\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3067\\u3001\\u305d\\u306e\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u3067\\u52d5\\u304f\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u6709\\u52b9\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3002\", \"constant\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u529b\\u306e\\u5b9a\\u6570 $K_k=\\\\partial^2E/\\\\partial Q_k^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3002\", \"intensity\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8d64\\u5916\\u5f37\\u5ea6 $I_k\\\\propto\\\\lvert\\\\partial\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}/\\\\partial Q_k\\\\rvert^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cc\\u6975\\u5b50\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30e1\\u30f3\\u30c8\\u306e\\u5909\\u5316\\u304b\\u3089\\u3002\", \"kind\": \"\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3092\\u6301\\u3064\\u3002\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u304c\\u306a\\u3044\\u3053\\u3068\\u3060\\u3051\\u3067\\u306f\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u8a00\\u3048\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u306e\\u6027\\u683c\": \"\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3092\\u6301\\u3064\\u3002\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u304c\\u306a\\u3044\\u3053\\u3068\\u3060\\u3051\\u3067\\u306f\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u8a00\\u3048\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"minimum\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u4f4e\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})=\\\\sum_A\\\\frac{Z_A}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{R}_A\\\\rvert}-\\\\int\\\\frac{\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime)}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime\\\\rvert}\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u5f15\\u304d\\u5bc4\\u305b\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\", \"maximum\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u9ad8\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u9000\\u3051\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\", \"Point\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u70b9\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"Q\": \"\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u3067\\u3001\\u5404\\u70b9\\u3067\\u56fa\\u5b9a\\u3059\\u308b\\u62d8\\u675f\\u4ed8\\u304d\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u5909\\u4f4d\\u3002\", \"Nitrogen distance\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u7a92\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"Oxygen distance\": \"\\u79fb\\u52d5\\u3059\\u308b\\u6c34\\u7d20\\u3068\\u9178\\u7d20\\u306e\\u9593\\u306e\\u8ddd\\u96e2\\u3002\", \"Energy\": \"\\u6bd4\\u8f03\\u306e\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc $\\\\Delta E=E-E_0$\\u3002\", \"Path energy\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411\\u7d4c\\u8def\\u306e\\u70b9 $s_\\\\mathrm{R}$ \\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u5dee $\\\\Delta E(s)=E(s)-E(s_\\\\mathrm{R})$\\u3002\\u305d\\u306e\\u70b9\\u304c\\u78ba\\u8a8d\\u6e08\\u307f\\u306e\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u4eee\\u5b9a\\u3057\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"Comparison energy\": \"\\u6700\\u5f8c\\u306b\\u8a18\\u9332\\u3057\\u305f\\u9006\\u65b9\\u5411 IRC \\u306e\\u70b9\\u306b\\u5bfe\\u3059\\u308b\\u96fb\\u5b50\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u3002\\u30b9\\u30ad\\u30e3\\u30f3\\u3084\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u306e\\u69cb\\u9020\\u306f IRC \\u4e0a\\u306b\\u3042\\u308b\\u3068\\u306f\\u9650\\u3089\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"Rms\": \"\\u4e8c\\u4e57\\u5e73\\u5747\\u5e73\\u65b9\\u6839\\u306e\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u52fe\\u914d $\\\\sqrt{\\\\frac{1}{3N}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{3N}(\\\\partial E/\\\\partial x_i)^2}$\\u3002$N$ \\u500b\\u306e\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u30c7\\u30ab\\u30eb\\u30c8\\u5ea7\\u6a19\\u306b\\u3064\\u3044\\u3066\\u53d6\\u308a\\u3001\\u505c\\u7559\\u70b9\\u3067\\u6d88\\u3048\\u308b\\u3002\", \"Mode\": \"\\u6700\\u521d\\u304b\\u3089\\u6570\\u3048\\u305f\\u57fa\\u6e96\\u632f\\u52d5\\u307e\\u305f\\u306f\\u8ecc\\u9053\\u5bfe\\u306e\\u756a\\u53f7\\u3002\", \"Frequency\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8abf\\u548c\\u6ce2\\u6570 $\\\\tilde\\\\nu_k=\\\\frac{1}{2\\\\pi c}\\\\sqrt{K_k/\\\\mu_k}$\\u3002\\u865a\\u6570\\u306e\\u5024\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u3067\\u793a\\u3057\\u3001\\u9077\\u79fb\\u72b6\\u614b\\u306e\\u3088\\u3046\\u306b\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u304c\\u4e0b\\u304c\\u308b\\u65b9\\u5411\\u3092\\u8868\\u3059\\u3002\", \"Mass\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u63db\\u7b97\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3067\\u3001\\u305d\\u306e\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u3067\\u52d5\\u304f\\u539f\\u5b50\\u306e\\u6709\\u52b9\\u8cea\\u91cf\\u3002\", \"Constant\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u529b\\u306e\\u5b9a\\u6570 $K_k=\\\\partial^2E/\\\\partial Q_k^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u30a8\\u30cd\\u30eb\\u30ae\\u30fc\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3002\", \"Intensity\": \"\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9 $k$ \\u306e\\u8d64\\u5916\\u5f37\\u5ea6 $I_k\\\\propto\\\\lvert\\\\partial\\\\boldsymbol{\\\\mu}/\\\\partial Q_k\\\\rvert^2$\\u3002\\u305d\\u308c\\u306b\\u6cbf\\u3063\\u305f\\u53cc\\u6975\\u5b50\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30e1\\u30f3\\u30c8\\u306e\\u5909\\u5316\\u304b\\u3089\\u3002\", \"Kind\": \"\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u30e2\\u30fc\\u30c9\\u306f\\u8ca0\\u306e\\u66f2\\u7387\\u3092\\u6301\\u3064\\u3002\\u865a\\u632f\\u52d5\\u304c\\u306a\\u3044\\u3053\\u3068\\u3060\\u3051\\u3067\\u306f\\u6975\\u5c0f\\u3068\\u306f\\u8a00\\u3048\\u306a\\u3044\\u3002\", \"Minimum\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u4f4e\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})=\\\\sum_A\\\\frac{Z_A}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{R}_A\\\\rvert}-\\\\int\\\\frac{\\\\rho(\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime)}{\\\\lvert\\\\mathbf{r}-\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime\\\\rvert}\\\\mathrm{d}\\\\mathbf{r}^\\\\prime$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u5f15\\u304d\\u5bc4\\u305b\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\", \"Maximum\": \"\\u5bc6\\u5ea6\\u66f2\\u9762\\u4e0a\\u306e\\u6700\\u3082\\u9ad8\\u3044\\u9759\\u96fb\\u30dd\\u30c6\\u30f3\\u30b7\\u30e3\\u30eb $V(\\\\mathbf{r})$ \\u3067\\u3001\\u8fd1\\u3065\\u304f\\u6b63\\u96fb\\u8377\\u304c\\u6700\\u3082\\u5f37\\u304f\\u9000\\u3051\\u3089\\u308c\\u308b\\u5834\\u6240\\u3092\\u793a\\u3057\\u307e\\u3059\\u3002\"}</script>");
